KG42.register("rules-d3eb951f31652692b4379533",{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R006","paper":"31-coalition_formation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R006","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Prosumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Prosumers without battery storage may participate in P2P trading and remain in state 1. Scope: Prosumer participation without battery storage in the proposed P2P scheme. Condition: The prosumer has no battery. Battery use for trading is optional: prosumers may participate in state 1 without charging or discharging their batteries for P2P trading. Scope: Prosumer participation in the proposed cooperative P2P trading framework.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.prosumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.prosumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Prosumer participation in the proposed cooperative P2P trading framework. | Prosumer participation without battery storage in the proposed P2P scheme.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g03-E27","v141-b-g03-E30"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Prosumers without battery storage may participate in P2P trading and remain in state 1. Scope: Prosumer participation without battery storage in the proposed P2P scheme. Condition: The prosumer has no battery.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E009","v141-b-g03-E30"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Battery use for trading is optional: prosumers may participate in state 1 without charging or discharging their batteries for P2P trading. Scope: Prosumer participation in the proposed cooperative P2P trading framework.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003","v141-b-g03-E27"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":null,"section":"1. Introduction","anchor_text":"al- prosumers. In particular, we use the framework of a cooperative game to [30] to capture the inte","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"State 1 refers to the state of a prosumer, in which it does not charge or discharge its battery for participating in P2P trading. It only uses its surplus generation for participating in the market. State 2 of a prosumer, on the other hand, refers to the state, in which it is willing to charge or discharge its battery for buying energy from or selling energy to the P2P market."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"a its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer in only buys energy, when ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We further consider that the prosumers participating in the P2P energy trading choose to be either of the two states at any given time slot t.\n(a) State 1 Prosumers in state 1 do not charge or discharge their batteries for trading purposes and only sell their surplus E_{n,sur}(t) to other prosumers in N\\{n\\} or to the grid when E_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - E_{n,pv}(t) > 0. In other words, a prosumer in state 1, which we denote as an element of set W, does not put its battery in the energy trading market. Similarly, a state 1 prosumer only buys energy, when necessary, to meet the deficient energy E_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - E_{n,hou}(t). Note that a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1.\n(b) State 2 Prosumers is state 2 use their batteries for trading purposes. That is, a prosumer in state 2, which we indicate via V is motivated, e.g., for more economical benefit, to discharge its battery for selling energy to other prosumers. Similarly, it may also buy energy from other peers to charge its battery for future needs.\nNote that when a prosumer does not have a battery (prosumer 6) or it does not want to charge or discharge despite having battery (prosumer 5 in time slot 1) will remain in state 1."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E27","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p11-c1r2__v141-a-M01-validation","page":11,"printed_page":null,"section":"5. Case study","anchor_text":"Fig. 5. Demonstration of opportunistic use of battery by dif Further, it is also important to note t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 5","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Further, it is also important to note that, as the cooperative framework is designed, the prosumers do not require to always use their batteries for participating in P2P trading. Rather, they can opportunistically choose to trade their battery energy when they find it beneficial for them by following (5) and (6) and still manage to reap a better (or at least equal) utility compared to the case without cooperation. For instance, as shown in Fig. 5, although a number prosumers are interested to trade their battery energy with other peers of the network (at time slots 25 to 45, for example), there is no trade of battery energy from any prosumers during time slots from 50 to 60. The benefit for P2P trading is, however, still obvious for time slots 50 to 60 as noted in Fig. 4. Such opportunistic use of battery helps prosumers to intelligently use their batteries for P2P trading without significantly compromising the lifetime of the batteries. Further, the proposed scheme may help prosumers to estimate how much they may need to invest on their batteries based on their frequency of battery usage for trading purposes (e.g., a prosumer do not need to buy a large battery if the result shows that it would be under used)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p11-c2r4__v141-a-M01-validation","page":11,"printed_page":null,"section":"6. Conclusion","anchor_text":"of by exploiting the social cooperation between different prosumers of the he network. For this purp","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"In this paper, we have studied a peer-to-peer energy trading scheme by exploiting the social cooperation between different prosumers of the network. For this purpose, we have proposed a coalition formation game that can help each participating prosumer to opportunistically decide whether it should put its battery in the peer-to-peer market for energy trading. It has been shown that the coalition structure that stems from prosumers’ social cooperation at each time slot is stable and the resultant peer-to-peer trading scheme is prosumer-centric. Further, we have conducted a number of case studies for the proposed scheme based on Australia based household energy usage and solar generation data and provided some numerical results to show that the proposed scheme can enable prosumers without any storage to participate and still benefit from peer-to-peer trading. Further, it has been demonstrated that the proposed trading scheme has the potential to help prosumers to intelligently use their batteries for peer-to-peer trading while considering the degradation cost of their battery. Here it is important to note the economic benefit could be different and more for the feed-in-tariff scheme if the feed-in-tariff rate is large enough. For example, when feed-in-tariff was first offered to the prosumers in Queensland, Australia, the rate was 44 cents per kWh. Nevertheless, such a high rate is not being offered anymore and the rate has been reduced significantly as articulated in numerous existing studies."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The source states participation eligibility and optional battery use qualitatively; it introduces no decision variable for this rule. Battery capacity b_n, state-of-charge s_n(t), and charging/discharging quantities e_{n,c}(t), e_{n,d}(t) belong to the paper's physical/utility/clearing rules, not to this frozen unary participation rule, and the frozen graph declares no variable objects for this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"No numeric parameter, coefficient, threshold, or constant is introduced by these participation statements. The source mentions no rule-specific battery-capacity value, price threshold, or other fixed input for the admission/optional-battery-use condition. Symbols from other rule scopes, such as p_{n,c}(t) and p_{n,d}(t), are not reused here without an explicit source definition scoped to this rule."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.prosumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E30","quote":"the proposed scheme can enable prosumers without any storage to participate and still benefit from peer-to-peer trading."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E009","quote":"Note that a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E27","quote":"the prosumers do not require to always use their batteries for participating in P2P trading."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","quote":"State 1 refers to the state of a prosumer, in which it does not charge or discharge its battery for participating in P2P trading."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"99bd837b127101b150791b19e9b4c3ff98607caa7944a53edf1136ecb0b787b9","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a qualitative prosumer-participation/admission rule: it states that prosumers without battery storage remain in state 1 and that battery use for P2P trading is optional. The supplied source text gives no equation, decision variable, threshold, coefficient, or optimization condition scoped specifically to this unary participation rule. This is not a declaration that the paper lacks mathematics elsewhere; other rules handle quantitative clearing, pricing, and utility expressions. B evidence remains unreviewed under the experiment policy.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"This admission/state constraint concerns the prosumer participation role represented by the frozen node participation.prosumer. The source states 'a prosumer without any battery always remains in state 1' and that the scheme can 'enable prosumers without any storage to participate'. No edge is present or needed for this unary participation rule, and no quantitative relation is asserted."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","node_ids":["participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"This optional-battery-use constraint also concerns only the prosumer participation role represented by participation.prosumer. The source states that prosumers 'do not require to always use their batteries for participating in P2P trading' and that state 1 'does not charge or discharge its battery for participating in P2P trading'. The frozen graph has no edge for this qualitative scope statement, and the source provides no formula specific to this rule."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
